    "<p>The <strong>quantile</strong> of order $p\\in(0, 1)$ is the number $x_p$ for which $F(x_p)=p$ (for increasing $F$; in general $x_p=\\inf\\{x: F(x)\\ge p\\}$).\n       $x_{0.5}$ is the <strong>median</strong>, $x_{0.25}$ and $x_{0.75}$ are the lower and upper <strong>quartiles</strong>. We find a quantile by solving the equation $F(x)=p$.</p>",
